      },
      "text": "Organizational change is where management theory meets political reality. Most change initiatives fail — not because the diagnosis is wrong or the solution is bad, but because the change process itself is mismanaged. Three distinct questions: How do you plan and sequence change? Why do people resist? How do organizations learn from the change? Each question has a different theoretical home."
